{"Denial cache blocks new access - Service.Check short-circuits to Allowed=false when the denial cache key exists, so a previously denied (namespace,user,action,name,folder) tuple will stay denied until the cache TTL expires even if the user gains permission in the meantime": 0.910528302192688, "List may serve stale results - Service.List returns the cached permission set on cache hit and never verifies it against the DB, so if the cache is outdated it can omit newly created/granted resources until TTL expiry": 0.7681756019592285, "Denial cache key delimiter collision - userPermDenialCacheKey function joins name and parent with underscore delimiters, but dashboard/folder UIDs can contain underscores, making field boundaries ambiguous and causing cached denial for one resource to incorrectly deny access to a different resource": 0.8665403723716736, "Missing metric on error path - In Check(), when getCachedIdentityPermissions succeeds but checkPermission returns an error, the function returns without incrementing the permissionCacheUsage metric, and when cache hits but permission is denied, it incorrectly records as cache miss": 0.9033827185630798, "DoS vector via denial cache bypass - An attacker can bypass the denial cache by requesting random or non-existent resource names, forcing a database query on every request and potentially causing Denial of Service and memory exhaustion in the cache": 0.6096285581588745}